        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// <para>This function writes exactly <c>size</c> bytes from the area pointed at by <c>ptr</c> to the stream. If this fails for any reason, it'll return less than <c>size</c> to demonstrate how far the write progressed. On success, it returns <c>size</c>.</para>
        /// <para>On error, this function still attempts to write as much as possible, so it might return a positive value less than the requested write size.</para>
        /// <para>The caller can use <see cref="CSDL.File.IOStream.Status">Status</see> to determine if the problem is recoverable, such as a non-blocking write that can simply be retried later, or a fatal error.</para>
        /// <para>A request for zero bytes on a valid stream will return zero immediately without accessing the stream, so the stream status (EOF, err, etc) will not change.</para>
        /// </remarks>
